$ two grids off the beam axis on bars (grid 7 at the root, 8 at the tip), so
$ that the surface spline sees the twist; CONM2 rotary inertias give the
$ bar its torsion (NASTRAN-95's bar mass carries none); the panel's
$ quarter chord sits 0.045 m ahead of the axis, so the bending-torsion
$ root crosses to flutter at about 62 m/s, k 1.3, and the torsion branch
$ diverges at about 104 m/s
